  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Pasted-Up Game Show",
    "overview": "Every surface is a set of paper slips cut out and pasted down. On the phone, the host laptop and the pack editor the slips sit on warm paper; on the TV they sit on a dark ink stage so they pop from across a room. Slips have hard 2–4 px ink outlines, hard offset shadows with no blur, and corners that are almost square. State is shown the way a zine would show it: rubber stamps with a word on them, a yellow highlighter pass behind \"you\", a ham-pink highlighter for wager clues, and one hand-drawn red marker stroke under a single heading per screen.\n\nThe system is HAM's organisation-wide System A (organization-docs/BRAND.md), specialised for a party game. It is dense where people operate (host console, editor), loud and sparse where people react (TV, buzzer), and always readable first: Atkinson Hyperlegible carries every word of UI, and Bricolage Grotesque at weight 800 is reserved for headings, scores and clue values. Decoration is cheap and physical (tape, tilt, a dot grid on the TV), never glossy: no gradients except the highlighter strips, no blur shadows, no glassmorphism, no rounded cards.\n\nMotion is short and paper-like: slips drop in, stamps thud down at a slight angle, the buzzer breathes while live. Nothing moves under reduced motion, and the one-shot \"Correct!\"/\"Incorrect\" feedback then holds still for its usual 2.4 s.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper (#f6f1e5) and surface (#fffdf6) grounds with near-black ink (#1c1a17) for text and 2 px borders.",
      "Hard offset shadows (2 px, 4 px, 6 px) in ink; on the TV, pure black or decorative red.",
      "Near-zero 2 px radius everywhere; only the buzzer is round.",
      "Stamps (uppercase, tracked, bordered, tilted −2°) carry state words.",
      "One accent each for meaning: blue = you can press it, green = correct, rust = incorrect, pink = Hot HAM!, yellow = attention or \"you\".",
      "Decorative red only as marker strokes, red stamp outlines, the TV starburst and shadow accents.",
      "The TV is a dark ink stage with a faint dot grid; everything on it scales in em from one root size."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Word-With-Color Rule",
        "body": "No color carries state alone. Every green has \"Correct\", every rust has \"Incorrect\" or a minus, every pink has \"Hot HAM!\" or \"Wager\", every yellow has a sentence.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Is Paint Rule",
        "body": "Marker red (#d93625) is 4.14:1 on paper. It decorates shapes and outlines only. If removing it would lose information, it was used wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Measured Pair Rule",
        "body": "Every text/background pair is listed in src/features/ui/contrast.ts and tested at 4.5:1 (text) or 3:1 (non-text). A new pair is added there before it ships.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wordmark Is Not Type Rule",
        "body": "\"HAM\" is always the traced wordmark SVG (currentColor fill). It is never set in Bricolage or any font, including inside \"Hot HAM!\".",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Display Face Earns Its Size Rule",
        "body": "Bricolage appears only at 1.375rem and up, or in numerals. Controls, labels and stamps stay in Atkinson.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Blur Rule",
        "body": "Shadows have zero blur radius. A soft shadow is a different brand.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Press-Into-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Pressable slips translate by their shadow offset on :active and lose the shadow. Nothing scales on press except the buzzer, which drops.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do put every color in :root in src/app/globals.css and add each new text/background pair to src/features/ui/contrast.ts.",
      "Do use a stamp with a word for every state, and keep stamp rotation within ±4°.",
      "Do use .btn--big for the single primary action on a screen and keep every phone tap target at least 44 px.",
      "Do size everything on the TV in em off .tv so 1366×768 and 1920×1080 keep the same composition.",
      "Do keep one red marker stroke per screen at most.",
      "Do stop all movement under prefers-reduced-motion, but keep one-shot judged feedback visible and still."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use marker red (#d93625) for text, links or any state signal.",
      "Don't add blurred shadows, gradients (other than the highlighter strip), glass effects or radii above 2 px (the buzzer excepted).",
      "Don't typeset \"HAM\" in a font; use the wordmark component.",
      "Don't use Bricolage for controls, labels, stamps or body text.",
      "Don't rotate cards or panels below 400 px wide.",
      "Don't let animation delay or gate a game action.",
      "Don't write \"Jeopardy\", \"Daily Double\" or \"Final Jeopardy\" anywhere."
